mptcp-bpf-dscp (1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pin a DSCP class to a set of MPTCP remote endpoint ids instead of one:
    the dscp_remote_id map becomes dscp_remote_ids, a 256-bit set of ids per
    class. A dual-stack router WAN has one id per address (+128/+192 for its
    IPv6 ones), and the router also sends id 0 for the WAN that opens the
    connections, the id the VPS knows the first subflow by. The map is
    renamed as a pinned map with the old value size cannot be reused.
  * mptcp-dscp-manager: "mptcp-scheduler-dscp.sh set <dscp> id <N>..."
    takes several ids, and keeps the first one when only the old single-id
    map is there.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:14:19 +0000

mptcp-bpf-dscp (1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version bump only, to keep the mptcp-bpf-* scheduler packages in step.
    No change to the scheduler itself.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

mptcp-bpf-dscp (1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the bpf_dscp MPTCP scheduler and its
    mptcp-scheduler-dscp.sh manager, for the server/VPS side of an
    OpenMPTCProuter multipath link. Adds the dscp_remote_id pinning
    mode (DSCP -> MPTCP remote endpoint id) needed there, since every
    subflow on the VPS shares the same local IP and can't be
    distinguished by dscp_iface's local-IP keying alone.

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
